{
  "description": "Linguistics lab organism — a Universal Grammar syntax-tree builder (learner assembles a sentence's constituent structure bottom-up, one labelled bracket at a time) and a historical sound-change stepper (learner applies ordered Great Vowel Shift rules and watches every matching word's pronunciation shift at once), composed from the std-ling-syntaxtree and std-ling-soundchange instrument atoms behind a mode router.",
